## General Formula

$$\boxed{u_n = \sum_{i \geq 0} \varepsilon_i\, 3^i, \quad \text{where } n = \sum_{i \geq 0} \varepsilon_i\, 2^i,\ \varepsilon_i \in \{0,1\}.}$$

Equivalently: **write $n$ in base $2$, then interpret the digit string as a base-$3$ number.**

The first few values: $u_0=0,\ u_1=1,\ u_2=3,\ u_3=4,\ u_4=9,\ u_5=10,\ u_6=12,\ u_7=13,\ u_8=27, \ldots$

